From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: smit1237 <smit1237@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 16:37:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 25/30] init: stop kills LXMF forked workers; daemons in own
 process groups; no held stdout

- rnsd, lxmd and nomadnet start in their own session/process group
  (setsid; pidfile == daemon pid == pgid). stop SIGTERMs the daemon,
  waits (bounded), then SIGKILLs the whole group and its logger, so
  LXMF's forked stamp workers can no longer be orphaned at 100% CPU.
  Workers never get SIGTERM: they inherit the daemon's handler and
  would rewrite LXMF state from a stale fork-time copy.
- No init script leaves a background child holding the caller's
  stdin/stdout/stderr (loggers, watchdog loops, udhcpc, dhcpcd, the
  delayed update check, resize2fs, adbd), so `S82rnsd restart | cat`
  and friends return promptly.
